/-- [D] Aristotle's ten Categories, in his order (Categories 4, 1b25-2a4). -/
inductive Category
  /-- substance (ousia, BFO independent continuant). What something is, standing on its own: this person, this house. Everything else is said of a substance or is in one (Categories 5, 2a11-b6). -/
  | «substance»
  /-- quantity (poson, BFO quality). How much or how many: a sum of money, hours, a weight (Categories 6). BFO treats a magnitude as a quality of its bearer. -/
  | «quantity»
  /-- quality (poion, BFO specifically dependent continuant). What sort: states and dispositions (a virtue, health, a skill), capacities, affective qualities and shape (Categories 8). Habits and virtues are qualities that last (8b27). -/
  | «quality»
  /-- relation (pros ti, BFO relational quality). Said of something toward another: friend of, citizen of, an end for the sake of which (Categories 7). -/
  | «relation»
  /-- place (pou, BFO site). Where: in the Lyceum, in Travis County (Categories 4, 2a1). A place holds what is in it (Physics IV.4). -/
  | «place»
  /-- time (pote, BFO temporal region). When: yesterday, last year (Categories 4, 2a2). -/
  | «time»
  /-- position (keisthai, BFO quality). How something lies or sits (Categories 4, 2a2). BFO treats a posture as a quality. -/
  | «position»
  /-- having (echein, BFO role). What one has on or holds: has shoes on, is armed (Categories 4, 2a3), and possessions, documents and rights (Categories 15). A need is a privation, the lack of a having (Categories 10, 12a26). BFO has no class for possession; holding something is modelled as a role. -/
  | «having»
  /-- doing (poiein, BFO process). Acting on something: cutting, working, buying (Categories 4, 2a3; 9). Doing and being affected are one change seen from agent and patient (Physics III.3, 202b). -/
  | «doing»
  /-- being affected (paschein, BFO process). Undergoing: being cut, being changed (Categories 4, 2a4; 9). Change is the actuality of what is potential, as such (Physics III.1, 201a10). -/
  | «beingAffected»
